1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,430
Teacher midterm practice, question 18.

2
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:07,111
A tensile specimen with a fifty millimeter gauge length

3
00:00:07,111 --> 00:00:10,060
and a twelve millimeter diameter is fractured.

4
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:13,343
Afterwards the gauge length is sixty eight millimeters,

5
00:00:13,343 --> 00:00:18,351
and the neck is six point four millimeters across. Which values are correct?

6
00:00:20,051 --> 00:00:24,945
Percent elongation compares lengths: sixty eight minus fifty, over fifty.

7
00:00:24,945 --> 00:00:26,836
That is thirty six percent.

8
00:00:27,456 --> 00:00:32,545
Percent reduction in area compares areas, and area goes as the diameter squared.

9
00:00:33,165 --> 00:00:36,110
Six point four squared is forty point nine six,

10
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:39,113
and twelve squared is one hundred forty four.

11
00:00:39,113 --> 00:00:42,866
So the reduction in area is seventy one point six percent.

12
00:00:44,466 --> 00:00:47,864
The answer is E: thirty six percent elongation, and

13
00:00:47,864 --> 00:00:51,031
seventy one point six percent reduction in area.

14
00:00:51,851 --> 00:00:56,418
Forty six point seven percent is the reduction in diameter, not area.

15
00:00:56,418 --> 00:00:58,017
Square the diameters.
